# ============================================================================
# annotate landing revamp — D2 Blueprint Ember — FULL PAGE
# Model: nano banana (gemini / gemini-2.5-flash-image) — pinned below.
# AI-GENERATED MEDIA: disclose as AI-generated when published.
# Gate A PASSED 2026-10-18 (user approved D1/D2/D3 generation).
# Copy: design/landing/COPY-v2.md §2 (headline + subhead + CTA pair).
# Run: generate-media-prompt design/landing/prompts/d2-blueprint-ember/full-page.media.prompt
# Text budget: 10 strings — the subhead is rendered truncated at its first
#   sentence for render legibility; the full approved subhead lives in
#   COPY-v2 §2. Ticket push is PLANNED: no ticket-creation card anywhere —
#   the roadmap row may carry only a tiny "Soon" chip.
# IA section order (approved): hero → try-it demo band → 7-step walkthrough →
#   features bento → embed snippet → for agents/MCP → roadmap → FAQ → final CTA.
# COPY CORRECTION 2026-10-18 (user): hero secondary CTA is now "Start free"
#   (was "Add to your site"); hero caption and embed heading added; the three
#   embed steps render as bars for text budget (full strings: COPY-v2 §10).
# Build-lane motion notes (not part of the render): grid lines fade in first
#   (200ms), then content; section labels tick into place like registration
#   targets; ember ring draw-on via stroke-dashoffset ~400ms.
# ============================================================================
schema: '0.4'
id: annotate-landing-blueprint-ember-fullpage
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Full-page desktop website mockup, tall portrait, a dark landing page drawn
    on an engineering drafting sheet: a faint blueprint grid of hairline lines
    #1C1C28 covers the near-black #0B0B10 background at very low contrast
    (barely visible, never fighting the content), evenly spaced, and each
    section sits inside crop-corner ticks with a tiny monospaced label bar.
    Top nav: wordmark reading exactly "annotate", in monospaced type, four
    gray nav-link bars, one ember pill button carrying no text. Hero splits
    left/right: left column has a monospaced
    eyebrow bar, the two-line large headline "Feedback that points at the
    thing.", a two-line muted subhead reading "annotate pins threaded comments
    to the exact element or text they're about." with both words "annotate"
    and "threaded" spelled exactly — the complete sentence, every word
    present, all in plain muted gray — ember button "Try it on this
    page" (spelled exactly) beside outlined button "Start free", plus a
    one-line small muted caption below the buttons reading "No signup to look
    around. To post or install: create an account, add your site, paste your
    tag."; right, a flat dark
    browser sheet floating on the grid with registration-style corner marks:
    title bar with three small GRAY dots, dark app page of gray placeholder
    bars, one "Export" button (spelled exactly) ringed in glowing ember with
    a small pin, a thin
    luminous orange connector to a monospaced comment thread card with two
    muted orange circle avatars and short bars, a thin orange arrow to a
    monospaced agent card reading "patch ready" (spelled exactly) with an
    orange check, and a tiny "Resolved" badge directly beneath that card. A
    dark instrument-panel comment rail with monospaced text bars and three
    short rows is flush-docked to the browser sheet's right edge
    with no gap. Below, sections in this exact order, each framed by
    crop-corner ticks: a wide live-demo band showing a dashed ring around one
    page element with a small pill; a single row of exactly seven small dark
    screenshot thumbnails sitting on grid cells; a six-tile bento of raised
    panels each
    with a tiny mono label bar and placeholder bars; a small heading "Add
    your site, get your tag" (spelled exactly) above a wide code panel holding
    only abstract gray bars of varied widths and indents — zero characters,
    no code — and one small icon-only copy button with no
    text label; a two-column text row
    with monospaced bars; a low roadmap row of small outline chips where
    exactly one tiny chip reads "Soon"; four slim textless accordion rows of
    gray bars with one small "FAQ" label beside them — the word FAQ appears
    exactly once, never on the bottom strip;
    a final textless ember-tinted strip with one ember button. The ONLY text in
    the whole image is exactly: annotate · Feedback that points at the thing.
    · annotate pins threaded comments to the exact element or text they're
    about. · Try it on this page · Start free · No signup to look around. To
    post or install: create an account, add your site, paste your tag. · Add
    your site, get your tag · Export · patch ready ·
    Resolved · Soon · FAQ. All other copy is abstract gray placeholder bars.
    Crisp Inter-style grotesque for the headline and buttons, true monospaced
    type for labels, high contrast, no warped text, calm and precise,
    generous negative space.
  negative: >-
    garbled glyphs, pseudo-letters, misspelled words, duplicated text, prices,
    dollar signs, currency, any real brand name or logo, URLs, hex codes, hash
    symbols, photographic people or faces, initials in avatars, blue or green
    glow, light theme, heavy visible grid, blueprint blue tint, graph paper,
    second saturated hue, ticket-creation card, Jira or tracker logo, lens
    flares, watermark, cluttered spacing, annoate or anobate misspellings of
    the wordmark, legible or semi-legible code characters, duplicated
    thumbnail rows, the string Add to your site, annocate, annobate, extra
    legible section labels such as LIVE DEMO or Roadmap
  style: >-
    dark-native flat UI illustration on a faint drafting grid, vector sharp,
    monospaced micro-labels, single warm ember accent #F97316, hairline
    borders, generous negative space

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions: {width: 832, height: 1248, aspect_ratio: '2:3'}

requirements:
  subject: complete dark landing page on a drafting substrate, nav to final
    CTA strip, hero with ringed element, comment thread, agent card, bento,
    snippet, roadmap, FAQ
  composition: faint grid visible across the page, crop-corner ticks frame
    each section, sections in approved order (hero, demo band, seven
    thumbnails, bento, snippet, agents row, roadmap, FAQ, strip); rail styled
    as instrument panel, flush-docked right; ember reserved for ring, pin,
    primary CTA
  palette: >-
    void #0B0B10, canvas #111118, surface #1A1A23, raised #23232E, mist
    #2A2A3A, grid #1C1C28, ember #F97316
  dont: [prices, brand logos, URLs, extra text, faces, second glow hue,
    heavy grid, ticket-creation imagery as a shipped step]

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  required_pass: [text_legibility, full_page_structure, accent_budget, grid_discipline]
  criteria:
    text_legibility: {weight: 3, description: exact string manifest, crisp, no garbled glyphs}
    full_page_structure: {weight: 3, description: nav, hero with CTAs, demo band, seven
      thumbnails, bento, snippet, agents row, roadmap with Soon chip, FAQ, final strip —
      present, ordered, rail attached}
    accent_budget: {weight: 2, description: only ring, pin and primary buttons are saturated orange}
    grid_discipline: {weight: 2, description: grid faint, below 5 percent contrast, never
      fights content — fails if grid dominates or disappears}
  reject_if: [garbled or misspelled text, price or currency symbol, third-party logo,
    light theme, detached floating rail, ticket-creation card shown as shipped,
    grid dominating the page]

tags: [marketing, landing-fullpage, annotate, blueprint-ember, ai-generated]
product_targets: [annotate.therobotlives.com]
